  <p>
    Mobile tyre fitting runs on a different rhythm to a fixed workshop — jobs are spread across postcodes, not bays,
    and a missed slot means a wasted drive rather than an empty bay. GarageCloud schedules mobile jobs on the same
    workshop board as fixed-site work, so a fitter's day is visible alongside everything else the business runs.
  </p>

  <h2>What a mobile tyre business needs from software</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Jobs scheduled and routed by location, not just by time slot.</li>
    <li>VRM lookup so a registration number pulls the right tyre size and vehicle details on site.</li>
    <li>Invoicing that can be raised and sent from the job, on the spot, not back at base.</li>
    <li>Service reminders for repeat customers, so a fleet or regular customer rebooks automatically.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Fixed site and mobile, in one system</h2>
  <p>
    Some mobile tyre fitters also run a bay or two at a fixed location. Rather than running two separate systems —
    one for the workshop, one for the van — GarageCloud puts mobile and in-bay jobs on the same board, with the same
    customer records, invoicing and reminders either way.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
